# The guided opening, as a player meets it: the standing goal, the key row under
# it, and what happens to that row when something is in front of you.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/guide.tour --seed=1 --hour=9 --weather=clear:0 --fit=glide_wing
#
# THIS TOUR EXISTS BECAUSE A SHOT CANNOT TAKE IT. `58_guide` sets
# `_off = options.shot != ""`, so the goal and the key row are switched off in
# every `tools/shot.sh` run and a picture of them can only ever be a tour. The
# key row was dead for every lesson in the game and fifteen green tests sat over
# it, because they all asked the guide and not one asked what the HUD had been
# handed. A frame is the only instrument that ever showed it.
#
# `--fit=glide_wing` is deliberate: a fitted ability grants an ACTION that
# nothing in the game named until now, so the wing is what makes that visible.
place spawn

# --- The goal stands; a lesson waits on the key row under it --------------------
# The goal says what to WANT and names no key -- core may not read a keyboard,
# and it said "(c)" until today. The key beside it is spelled off the live
# InputMap, so this frame is also the proof that rebinding would move it.
wait 2.6
shot 01-the-goal-stands-and-a-lesson-waits-under-it

# --- The goal follows the player; the lesson has not been spent yet -------------
# Walking away from the village fire changes what to want. The lesson on the row
# is the SAME one: the row shows the first lesson not yet retired, and the guide
# spends one line per interval, so a goal that changed takes this turn.
walk 1,0 2.0
wait 3.0
shot 02-the-goal-changes-and-the-lesson-holds-its-place

# --- What is in front of you outranks a lesson on the row -----------------------
# Standing at driftwood, the row belongs to the thing under your hand and the
# lesson moves to the message line, still carrying its own key. Staged BY NAME,
# so the frame survives the next change to worldgen.
at prop:driftwood
wait 3.0
shot 03-what-is-in-front-of-you-takes-the-row

# --- The teaching channel a person is ------------------------------------------
# docs/DESIGN.md §Safe havens: "the teaching lives in the place, not on the glass.
# A lesson is somebody who lives there." Walked to on the real move path and asked
# with the real `use` key.
#
# **THIS FRAME HOLDS A SCRIPTED TALK, AND IT IS NAMED FOR THAT.** It was called
# "somebody who lives here teaches you" and showed a digger's sub-arc instead --
# a frame proving the opposite of its own name, which is the thing the claims
# test exists for. `walkto folk` takes whoever the camera can see, and the one it
# reached had words of her own. The teaching FALLBACK is the same key on a
# villager who has none: measured on seed 4, two of six villagers have nothing
# scripted, so the path is reachable and not dead -- but a tour cannot ask for
# "a villager with nothing written", so it is held by
# tests/survival/test_guide.gd rather than pretended at here.
village 0
wait 1.0
walkto folk 8
tap use
wait 0.9
shot 04-a-person-here-has-words-of-her-own with folk
